---
import TrustPage from "../components/trust/TrustPage.astro";
import { routeIndexable } from "../lib/indexability";
---

<TrustPage
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy for this site. No form provider, analytics, or lead sharing is configured."
  noindex={!routeIndexable("/privacy")}
>
  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    Golden Visa Research is a static website. The pages are files. The site does not run an account system.
  </p>
  <h2>Data destinations in this build</h2>
  <p>
    Fonts are files served with the site: Source Serif 4 and Inter, in Latin and Latin Extended. There is no analytics script, no advertising cookie set by the site code, and no social widget.
  </p>
  <p>
    An audit page can show a video. The still image is a file on this site. The video is provided by a third party once the reader chooses play. Opening the page does not contact that provider.
  </p>
  <p>
    Newsletter, contact, and correction forms have no form provider. Their endpoints are empty. Submitting one does not send the fields to Formspree or to any other company. No newsletter list exists.
  </p>
  <p>
    An article can include one inquiry form. The form asks for an email address, a LinkedIn profile URL, and one program of interest. It also carries the article title, the article URL, and the source name GoldenVisaResearch.com. No inquiry endpoint is configured. Submitting the form does not send or store those fields, and it does not add the address to a newsletter list.
  </p>
  <p>
    No commercial introduction and no lead-sharing arrangement are recorded.
  </p>
  <h2>Separate choices</h2>
  <p>
    A newsletter subscription asks for an email address and a separate confirmation that the address may be used for the newsletter. Sending a contact message, a correction report, or an article inquiry does not opt the sender into that list.
  </p>
  <h2>What is not recorded</h2>
  <p>
    No legal entity, postal address, privacy contact, retention period, or hosting contract is recorded. This page does not copy another organization's privacy policy. If a Formspree form ID is approved later, the fields on that form would go to Formspree, and this page would have to name that destination before the form is allowed to submit.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
